  "summary": "Preprints and a published study add three-dimensional binding context to sequence and ligand models for interfaces, ternary complexes and pockets.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is supplying three-dimensional and binding-partner context to models that otherwise operate on sequence or on isolated ligand-protein pairs. HandShake (PLoS Computational Biology) combines ProstT5 with LoRA tuning, cross-chain attention and contact supervision to predict partner-specific protein-protein binding sites from sequence alone. DiffTernary applies a diffusion model to docking molecular glue ternary complexes and introduces Ternary-PDB, a curated set of 76,702 PDB ternary structures. PocketVec pocket-similarity descriptors map 51,535 druggable human pockets to select diverse targets for Target 2035 ligand dataset generation. The emphasis across these studies falls on partner-specific and complex-level modeling, with structural information entering through explicit interface and complex supervision. The PocketVec study is a dataset-construction tool rather than a language model, so this thread is dominant rather than shared by every study.",
